# The build context is `box/software/` — this directory, not the repo root: `build-release.sh`
# derives its root from its own location and cd's here before invoking buildx, which is also why
# every path below is written relative to this file. Everything the release needs is either
# committed or generated inside the container.
#
# node_modules is the important one: the host tree holds darwin binaries (sharp, rolldown,
# oxlint), and `COPY . .` would drop them on top of the arm64 tree npm just built.
node_modules/
dist/
coverage/
release/
build/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Device state and generated audio — rebuilt in the image by `npm run sounds`.
#
# Note what is NOT excluded: `src/audio/samples/*.mp3`. Those are the designed recordings
# three of the cues are mastered from, and `npm run sounds` runs inside the image — excluding
# them here fails the build at build:assets with a missing cue, not with a missing MP3.
data/
src/audio/sounds/
*.ogg
*.wav

.git/
.github/
.claude/
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.log

# Secrets must never enter a build context.
auth_info*/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
